    "['vrrp vrid [parameter1] track interface [parameter2] reduced [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/3 unit 0 family inet address 10.0.0.1/24 vrrp-group 10 track interface ge-1/0/2 priority-cost 50', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the given HUAWEI VRRP tracking command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/3 unit 0 family inet address 10.0.0.1/24 vrrp-group 10 track interface ge-1/0/2 priority-cost 50\\n##\\n\\nThis Juniper command:\\n1. Configures tracking on interface ge-1/0/2\\n2. Associates it with VRRP group 10\\n3. Sets the priority reduction to 50 if the tracked interface goes down\\n4. Maintains the same IP address configuration as in the original\\n5. Assumes ge-1/0/3 is using unit 0 (default) with family inet (IPv4)\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, VRRP configuration is nested under the interface's address family configuration rather than being separate commands as in HUAWEI.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/3 unit 0 family inet address 10.0.0.1/24 vrrp-group 10 track interface ge-1/0/2 priority-cost 50'}]]": 1,
