    "['service-instance-group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set services service-set SS21 next-hop-service inside-service-interface s-1/0/0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set services service-set SS21 next-hop-service inside-service-interface s-1/0/0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Based on the Huawei configuration context, the `service-instance-group` command is used to associate a service location with an instance group (likely for CGN/NAT purposes). In Juniper, the equivalent would typically involve creating a service-set or NAT rule-set.\\n\\nFor Juniper MX Series (with services like NAT/CGN), the closest equivalent would be a `service-set` configuration. Here's the translation:\\n\\n##\\nset services service-set SS21 next-hop-service inside-service-interface s-1/0/0.0\\nset services service-set SS21 next-hop-service outside-service-interface s-1/0/1.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact Juniper equivalent depends on the specific service being implemented (DS-Lite in this case). A more precise translation might require additional Juniper-specific DS-Lite configuration blocks. The above assumes a basic service-set configuration for NAT/CGN services.\\n\\nWould you like me to provide a more specific DS-Lite translation for Juniper instead?\", 'trans_template': 'set services service-set SS21 next-hop-service inside-service-interface s-1/0/0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set services service-set SS21 next-hop-service outside-service-interface s-1/0/1.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set services service-set SS21 next-hop-service outside-service-interface s-1/0/1.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Based on the Huawei configuration context, the `service-instance-group` command is used to associate a service location with an instance group (likely for CGN/NAT purposes). In Juniper, the equivalent would typically involve creating a service-set or NAT rule-set.\\n\\nFor Juniper MX Series (with services like NAT/CGN), the closest equivalent would be a `service-set` configuration. Here's the translation:\\n\\n##\\nset services service-set SS21 next-hop-service inside-service-interface s-1/0/0.0\\nset services service-set SS21 next-hop-service outside-service-interface s-1/0/1.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact Juniper equivalent depends on the specific service being implemented (DS-Lite in this case). A more precise translation might require additional Juniper-specific DS-Lite configuration blocks. The above assumes a basic service-set configuration for NAT/CGN services.\\n\\nWould you like me to provide a more specific DS-Lite translation for Juniper instead?\", 'trans_template': 'set services service-set SS21 next-hop-service outside-service-interface s-1/0/1.0'}]]": 1,
